dimensions_checked.result:
m3: the top-key step misses three things it needs to work:
- the Drive split regex and the hasTopLive branch;
- the Normal-priority Ui() call racing the Loaded restore;
- how long New-TopsTree's scan stays live.
m5: guard 5 names no WindowCases case.
m6: the stale guard may also skip the existing LastRefresh and _skipNextRefresh lines.

None beyond m6. The design handles:
- a null container (focus stays on the list, no cast, no scroll);
- a replaced or nulled ItemsSource (ReferenceEquals guard);
- a null FocusedElement;
- a missing key.
An exception in the Loaded callback would reach the dispatcher, and Q-071 forbids a global Handled=true, but nothing in the restore plausibly throws.

The design respects:
- the KnownWorkarounds policy (own-code defect, no checkbox);
- Q-114 (WindowMutants required);
- lessons #91 (ASCII), #136 (network pass stated as unmeasured), #336 (R-001 person-run), #391/#392 (TEMP wrapper) and #405 (serial runs).
The only gap is m4: the required WindowMutants run gives no signal on this change.
